{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Aenima and Lateralus feel like natural next choices after 10.000 Days because I want more Tool, especially the heavy riffs, intricate rhythms, and immersive songs.",
    "American Idiot connects with the energetic guitars I enjoyed in Chuck and Fefe Dobson. The Young and the Hopeless also fits that side of my listening, although I would choose something heavier now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "X&Y and How to Dismantle An Atomic share a broad rock connection with my history, but their softer or arena-rock sound does not satisfy my current interest in heavier, more intricate music.",
    "Kid A's electronic atmosphere, The Piper at the Gates of Dawn's psychedelia, and the hip-hop and dance-pop selections do not offer the heavy guitar sound I am looking for now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in some melodic rock seems to have been taken as interest in rock broadly, even though guitar weight and rhythmic intensity matter to my choices.",
    "The selections feel too centered on familiar albums from roughly the same era as my listening; sharing a period does not make them fit the sound I want."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest choices, Ten Thousand Fists and 10.000 Days, make heavy riffs and intricate rhythms especially relevant right now.",
    "My repeated listening to albums such as Colony, Reroute to Remain, and Soundtrack to Your Escape suggests a sustained appetite for heavier music, while my earlier pop-punk interests are only part of the picture."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The Tool recommendations understand my current direction, but much of the rest treats my broader listening history as more relevant than my present preference for heavy, intricate guitar music."
}"}
